/* Deep aspect interpretations, part 1: pairs led by Sun, Moon, Mercury and Venus */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.aspects1 = {
  "sun|moon": {
    theme: "Your conscious purpose and your emotional needs have to find a working agreement. The Sun wants direction and self-expression, while the Moon asks for safety, comfort and rhythm. How well they cooperate shapes your basic sense of wholeness.",
    fusion: "Born near a New Moon, you tend to feel what you want and want what you feel, with little gap between the two. This gives you a single-minded quality and a strong instinct for your own path. The catch is subjectivity: it can be hard to step outside your own mood and see how others experience you. A trusted outside view helps.",
    flow: "Your head and heart generally speak the same language, which gives you a steady, self-accepting core. Other people often find you easy to be around because you are not fighting yourself. Decisions about home and ambition rarely pull in opposite directions. The risk is complacency: inner comfort can keep you from stretching into the harder growth that would sharpen you.",
    tension: "What you set out to do and what you need to feel secure often seem to argue. You might push hard toward a goal, then feel drained and resentful, or retreat into comfort and feel you have lost your edge. Partners can end up carrying one side of the split. Integration comes when you schedule rest into ambition and let feelings inform your plans."
  },
  "sun|mercury": {
    theme: "Your identity and your thinking sit very close together in every chart, since Mercury never strays far from the Sun. The question is how much space your mind has to observe you, rather than simply speak for you.",
    fusion: "Your thoughts and your sense of self are tightly bound, so ideas feel personal and you speak with conviction. You often think out loud and can be a persuasive advocate for what you believe. Close to the Sun, though, Mercury can lose objectivity, and criticism of an idea may sting like criticism of you. Learning to hold opinions a little more loosely widens your thinking.",
    flow: "Where Mercury sits in its own sign apart from the Sun, your mind gains a little distance from your ego. You can explain yourself clearly, and you tend to learn by talking things through. Writing, teaching and negotiation often come naturally. Because words come easily, you may skip the slower work of checking facts or listening fully before you answer.",
    tension: "Friction here is subtle, since the two never form a true square. It tends to show as a gap between what you mean and what you manage to say, or a habit of rushing speech ahead of reflection. Others may misread your intent. Pausing before replying and writing things down first helps your words carry the weight of who you are."
  },
  "sun|venus": {
    theme: "Your core self and your capacity for pleasure, beauty and love must learn to share the stage. Venus stays close to the Sun, so the task is balancing self-expression with the wish to be liked.",
    fusion: "Charm and identity are woven together here. You tend to radiate warmth, enjoy beautiful things, and draw people in without much effort. Art, style or hospitality may feel central to who you are. The shadow is a strong need for approval, which can make conflict uncomfortable and lead you to smooth things over rather than state your real position.",
    flow: "With Venus a little apart from the Sun, affection and self-worth support each other quietly. You usually know what you value and can enjoy life without guilt. Relationships and creative work tend to flow. Because pleasure and goodwill come fairly easily, you may avoid effort or unpleasant truths that would give your talents more depth and staying power.",
    tension: "True squares cannot form between these two, so strain shows up more gently, as a sense that being loved and being yourself pull slightly apart. You might tone yourself down to keep the peace, or feel undervalued when others miss your effort. Recognising your own worth without waiting for applause lets the two energies settle into an honest partnership."
  },
  "sun|mars": {
    theme: "Your sense of purpose and your drive to act have to agree on direction and pace. The Sun gives the reason, Mars supplies the push, and the relationship between them colours how you assert yourself.",
    fusion: "Will and action arrive together here, so you tend to move quickly once you know what you want. You often have abundant energy, courage and a competitive streak that helps you start things. The same fire can make you impatient or combative when blocked. Physical outlets and clear goals keep the heat productive rather than scorching the people close to you.",
    flow: "Your drive works in step with your identity, so you tend to act confidently without much internal debate. Sport, leadership, or any work that rewards initiative can feel natural. People see you as capable and direct. Because action comes easily, you may rely on momentum and bravado instead of strategy, and occasionally charge ahead before checking that the fight is worth having.",
    tension: "Your purpose and your temper do not always line up. You may swing between holding back and then erupting, or pick fights that pull you away from what you really want. In relationships, anger can surface suddenly over small things. Integration means learning to name frustration early and aiming your considerable force at a chosen target instead of whoever is nearest."
  },
  "sun|jupiter": {
    theme: "Your identity meets the urge to grow, believe and expand. The negotiation is between healthy confidence and inflation, between faith in yourself and knowing where your limits genuinely lie.",
    fusion: "Optimism is built into your sense of self. You tend to think big, attract opportunities and lift the mood of a room. Generosity and a sense of meaning often drive you. The difficulty is excess: overcommitting, overpromising or assuming things will work out without the groundwork. Pairing your vision with realistic follow-through turns natural luck into lasting achievement.",
    flow: "Goodwill and good timing tend to follow you. You recover from setbacks with humour, and people like helping you. Teaching, travel, publishing or anything that broadens horizons may come easily. Because doors often open without much effort, you can coast on charm or potential and leave talents half developed. Choosing a direction and committing to it deepens your gift.",
    tension: "Your appetite for more can clash with what serves you. You may overreach, promise too much, or swing between grand plans and disappointment when reality falls short. Others may see you as self-important at times, even when you mean well. Growth comes from matching belief with discipline and learning that enough can be as meaningful as more."
  },
  "sun|saturn": {
    theme: "Your self-expression meets the demand for structure, responsibility and time. Saturn tests the Sun, and the negotiation is between who you want to be and what you are willing to earn.",
    fusion: "Seriousness and ambition shape your core. You often feel older than your years and carry an early sense of duty, perhaps linked to a demanding or absent father figure. Self-doubt can be strong in youth. With time, this becomes remarkable staying power: you build things properly, and your authority grows steadily. Allowing yourself pleasure along the way prevents hardness.",
    flow: "Discipline supports your identity instead of crushing it. You tend to be reliable, patient and good at long-term planning, and people trust your judgement. Structure feels steadying. Because you manage responsibility so well, others may lean on you heavily, and you may play safe when a bolder move would serve you. Letting yourself take calculated risks keeps you growing.",
    tension: "An inner critic often questions your right to shine. You may feel blocked by authority figures or by your own harsh standards, and success can seem to come late or at great cost. Defensiveness or rigidity may show in relationships. Integration arrives when you become your own fair authority, setting realistic goals and recognising the strength that years of effort have built."
  },
  "sun|uranus": {
    theme: "Your core identity meets the pull toward freedom, originality and sudden change. The question is how to be authentically different while still having a stable centre others can rely on.",
    fusion: "Independence is part of your nature. You tend to think unconventionally, resist being told what to do, and feel most alive when breaking new ground. Friends see you as refreshing, sometimes unpredictable. Restlessness can lead to abrupt exits from jobs or relationships. Learning to distinguish genuine calling from simple contrariness lets your originality serve something lasting.",
    flow: "Innovation comes naturally, and you can introduce new ideas without alienating people. You are often comfortable with technology, groups or causes, and you adapt quickly when circumstances shift. Your individuality feels relaxed. Because change comes easily, you may undervalue consistency, drifting between interests or avoiding the slow commitment that would let your inventive streak produce real results.",
    tension: "Your need for freedom and your need for a coherent identity often clash. You might rebel against structures you also depend on, or experience sudden disruptions that force you to rethink who you are. Partners can feel kept at a distance. Integration involves creating room for independence inside commitments, so change becomes a choice rather than an explosion."
  },
  "sun|neptune": {
    theme: "Your sense of self meets the longing to dissolve into something larger. The task is balancing clear identity with imagination, compassion and spiritual sensitivity, without losing your outline altogether.",
    fusion: "Your identity has a porous, imaginative quality. You often absorb atmospheres, feel other people's pain, and are drawn to art, music, healing or spirituality. Others may project their fantasies onto you. The challenge is definition: knowing what you want, and not idealising people or escaping when life gets hard. Creative discipline gives this sensitivity a reliable channel.",
    flow: "Imagination and intuition support your sense of self gently. You tend to have artistic flair, empathy and a feel for the unseen, and people find you kind. Inspiration arrives without strain. Because it arrives so easily, you may drift, waiting for the right mood instead of practising the craft. A little structure turns your dreaminess into genuine creative work.",
    tension: "Clarity about who you are can blur under pressure. You might idealise people, feel deceived, or doubt your direction after disappointments. Escapism through fantasy, overwork or substances can tempt. In relationships, boundaries may become confused. Integration means grounding compassion in realistic assessment, and trusting your intuition while still checking the facts before committing yourself."
  },
  "sun|pluto": {
    theme: "Your identity meets forces of power, depth and transformation. The negotiation is between self-expression and the urge to control, and between surviving intensity and allowing it to renew you.",
    fusion: "You carry an intense presence that people notice even when you are quiet. Your will is strong, and you rarely do anything halfway. Life may bring crises that strip away old versions of yourself. There can be a pull toward control or secrecy. Used consciously, this gives you tremendous resilience and the ability to transform situations others consider hopeless.",
    flow: "Depth and determination support you without overwhelming you. You often have a talent for research, psychology or strategy, and you can handle crises calmly. People sense your quiet strength. Because this power feels ordinary to you, you may underestimate its effect on others or avoid the deeper emotional work that would bring it fully to life.",
    tension: "Power struggles often mark this contact, with authority figures, partners or your own compulsions. You may swing between feeling powerless and wanting total control. Intensity can frighten people, or you may fear it yourself. Integration comes through honest self-examination, letting go of what has died, and using your formidable will to empower rather than dominate."
  },
  "sun|chiron": {
    theme: "Your sense of self meets a core wound that asks for understanding. The negotiation is between shining openly and protecting a tender place, and between hiding the hurt and turning it into wisdom.",
    fusion: "Your identity is bound up with a wound, often around confidence, recognition or the right to exist as you are. You may have felt overlooked early on. This sensitivity can make you a gifted mentor, because you understand struggle from the inside. The risk is defining yourself only by pain. Letting healing be part of your story, not the whole of it, frees you.",
    flow: "Your vulnerabilities and strengths cooperate. You tend to speak about difficulty without shame, and others find it easy to open up to you. Teaching, coaching or care work may suit you. Because this empathy comes naturally, you might give it away freely while neglecting your own healing. Remember to receive the kind of support you offer others.",
    tension: "A sore spot around self-worth can flare when you try to shine. You might overcompensate with bravado or shrink back before you can be rejected. Criticism may land hard. Relationships can reopen old wounds. Integration involves meeting your hurt with patience, noticing when it drives your choices, and allowing your hard-won understanding to become a source of authority."
  },
  "sun|northNode": {
    theme: "Your core purpose meets the direction of growth your soul is reaching toward. The negotiation is whether your natural self-expression helps you move forward or keeps you circling familiar ground.",
    fusion: "Your identity and life direction are closely aligned. You often feel that simply being yourself moves you toward purpose, and others may see you as someone with a clear path. Visibility can come early. The challenge is that growth still requires effort: identifying with destiny can breed impatience. Staying humble and curious lets this alignment unfold steadily.",
    flow: "Your personal strengths support your growth quite naturally. Opportunities that fit your development often appear when you act confidently. Mentors and allies can be helpful. Because this support feels easy, you might not notice when you are coasting. Checking periodically whether you are stretching toward new territory keeps this gift from becoming mere comfort.",
    tension: "Your ego and your growth path can seem to disagree. You might feel that what makes you shine is exactly what you need to outgrow, or you may default to safe habits instead of the unfamiliar lessons calling you. Integration involves bringing your confidence and warmth into new territory, letting your identity expand to include what you are learning."
  },
  "sun|lilith": {
    theme: "Your identity meets the raw, untamed part of you that refuses to be domesticated. The question is how to express your wild edge and your anger at injustice without being exiled for it.",
    fusion: "A fierce independence sits at your core. You tend to resist social expectations, especially around gender, sexuality or authority, and you can be magnetic and provocative. Some people feel threatened by your intensity. You may have experienced rejection for being too much. Owning this raw energy with pride, instead of hiding or flaunting it, becomes a real source of power.",
    flow: "Your untamed side integrates quite comfortably with your identity. You can speak uncomfortable truths without much fear, and your authenticity often inspires others. Taboo topics feel manageable to you. Because this edge comes easily, you may not notice when it wounds, or you might settle into a rebel persona that stops you exploring your gentler sides.",
    tension: "Parts of you that feel shameful or forbidden may clash with how you want to be seen. You might suppress anger or desire until it bursts out, or feel pushed to the margins. Relationships can trigger fears of being rejected for your raw self. Integration involves reclaiming this energy consciously and letting your full self take up space."
  },
  "sun|asc": {
    theme: "Your inner identity meets the way you present yourself to the world. The negotiation is between who you are inside and the first impression you create when you walk into a room.",
    fusion: "What people see is largely who you are. Your presence is clear and often strong, and you tend to be recognised quickly. Self-expression feels natural, and leading may come easily. The downside is a certain self-focus, or difficulty stepping back and letting others shine. Checking in with how people experience you helps keep this vivid presence generous.",
    flow: "Your inner self and outer manner work well together. People usually get an accurate sense of you quickly, which builds trust. You can adapt your style without losing authenticity. Because this coherence feels effortless, you may not appreciate how much it helps you, or you might rely on first impressions instead of developing depth over time.",
    tension: "Your outer manner and your inner identity can seem mismatched. People may misjudge you, and you might feel pulled between being yourself and being agreeable. In partnerships, you may define yourself through the other person. Integration comes when you let your real purpose shape your presentation, allowing others to meet the person underneath your social face."
  },
  "sun|mc": {
    theme: "Your core self meets your public role and ambitions. The negotiation is between personal fulfilment and reputation, and between shining for your own reasons and seeking recognition from the world.",
    fusion: "Visibility and career are central to your identity. You tend to want your work to reflect who you are, and recognition often comes through a public role. Leadership may feel natural. The risk is tying self-worth too tightly to status or achievement. Remembering that you have value outside your title lets you enjoy success without being defined by it.",
    flow: "Your ambitions and personality support each other. Career choices tend to fit you, and authority figures may help you. You often find a public role that feels authentic. Because professional progress comes naturally, you may not push yourself toward the most meaningful work. Asking what truly matters to you keeps success aligned with purpose.",
    tension: "Private life and public life can pull hard against each other. You might feel your career demands a version of you that is not quite real, or home responsibilities may compete with ambition. Integration involves defining success on your own terms and letting personal values shape your public direction, rather than performing a role that drains you."
  },
  "moon|mercury": {
    theme: "Feeling and thinking have to learn each other's language. The Moon reacts from instinct and memory, Mercury names and analyses, and together they shape how you talk about what you feel.",
    fusion: "Your thoughts are coloured by mood, and your moods quickly become words. You often remember emotional details, pick up on tone, and write or speak with warmth. Conversation can be how you process feelings. The difficulty is objectivity: it may be hard to separate facts from how you feel about them, and anxious thinking can loop late at night.",
    flow: "Head and heart communicate easily in you. You can explain your feelings without drama and listen well when others share theirs. This makes you a natural confidant, writer or carer. Because emotional articulacy comes so readily, you may talk around feelings instead of sitting with them, or assume understanding something is the same as having felt it through.",
    tension: "What you think and what you feel often disagree. You might rationalise emotions away, or find your reasoning hijacked by a mood. Loved ones can feel you say one thing while signalling another. Nervous tension may show in restless sleep or overthinking. Integration grows when you let feelings be felt first, then give them words without judgement."
  },
  "moon|venus": {
    theme: "Your need for security meets your capacity for pleasure and affection. The two must agree on what comfort means, and on how you give and receive care in close relationships.",
    fusion: "Tenderness is central to your emotional nature. You tend to create beautiful, comfortable surroundings and show love through small, thoughtful gestures. People often find you soothing. The challenge is dependence on harmony: you may avoid conflict, over-indulge in food or spending for comfort, or need constant reassurance. Learning that love can survive disagreement strengthens your bonds.",
    flow: "Affection and emotional security support each other gently. You often have a gift for hospitality, a good eye for colour and texture, and an easy way with people. Relationships tend to feel nourishing. Because warmth comes naturally, you may drift toward comfort and avoid situations that ask you to grow, confront or risk a little.",
    tension: "What makes you feel safe and what you find attractive can pull apart. You might be drawn to partners who do not quite meet your emotional needs, or feel torn between caring for others and enjoying yourself. Comfort-seeking can become excessive. Integration involves recognising both needs as valid and choosing relationships that honour security and delight together."
  },
  "moon|mars": {
    theme: "Your emotional needs meet your drive to act and assert. The negotiation is between protecting yourself and pushing forward, and between feeling safe and feeling free to show anger.",
    fusion: "Feelings turn into action very quickly for you. You tend to react strongly, defend loved ones fiercely, and wear your emotions openly. There is great protective courage here. The same speed can mean flashes of temper or defensiveness, especially when you feel vulnerable. Learning to pause between feeling and reacting gives your passion more reach and fewer regrets.",
    flow: "Emotional courage comes naturally to you. You can stand up for yourself and others without much internal struggle, and you usually act on your instincts effectively. Physical activity can help you process feelings. Because this energy flows readily, you may push through emotions instead of feeling them, or become impatient with people who process more slowly.",
    tension: "Anger and vulnerability often collide. You might feel irritable when you most need comfort, or snap at people you love when you feel unsafe. Home life can become a battleground. Integration comes through recognising anger as information about unmet needs, finding healthy outlets for frustration, and learning to ask for support directly instead of fighting for it."
  },
  "moon|jupiter": {
    theme: "Your emotional nature meets the urge to expand and find meaning. The negotiation is between generous feeling and emotional excess, and between faith that things will be fine and honest attention to real needs.",
    fusion: "Emotional generosity defines you. You tend to feel deeply, give freely, and create a sense of abundance around you. Family and cultural roots can mean a lot. The challenge is excess: overeating, overspending or overpromising when emotions run high. Your optimism is a real gift. Grounding it in practical limits helps it nourish you and others long term.",
    flow: "You tend to meet life with emotional buoyancy. Setbacks rarely keep you down, and people feel uplifted in your company. Generosity, humour and faith come easily. Because good feeling is your default, you may skim over sadness or avoid the harder emotional work that would deepen your wisdom. Allowing grief its place enriches your natural warmth.",
    tension: "Emotional needs and larger ambitions can compete. You might feel restless at home, craving more, or swing between emotional highs and disappointments. Overindulgence can become a way of soothing unease. Integration involves finding meaning within ordinary daily life, and learning that you can grow without constantly needing more stimulation or reassurance."
  },
  "moon|saturn": {
    theme: "Your need for comfort meets the demands of discipline and responsibility. The task is allowing yourself tenderness while also building the emotional maturity to hold difficult feelings steadily.",
    fusion: "Emotional reserve runs deep here. You may have taken on responsibility early or felt that care was conditional. As a result, you often manage feelings privately and appear composed. Loneliness can sit underneath. With time, this contact gives remarkable emotional steadiness and loyalty. Letting trusted people see your softness gradually eases the old expectation that you must cope alone.",
    flow: "You bring calm maturity to emotional situations. People rely on you in a crisis, and you can manage stress without falling apart. Routines and commitments feel steadying. Because you handle responsibility so well, you may become the carer who never asks for care, or treat feelings as problems to manage instead of experiences to share.",
    tension: "Needs and duties often seem at odds. You might feel guilty resting, or struggle to ask for comfort, expecting disappointment. Coldness or depression can surface under pressure. Relationships may carry echoes of a distant or strict parent. Integration comes when you parent yourself with patience, allowing support in and treating your needs as legitimate responsibilities too."
  },
  "moon|uranus": {
    theme: "Your need for emotional security meets the urge for freedom and change. The negotiation is between closeness and independence, and between comfort in routine and excitement in the unexpected.",
    fusion: "Your emotions are quick, surprising and sometimes hard to predict, even for you. You often need a lot of personal space and can feel stifled by traditional domestic life. Friends may know you as original and emotionally honest. The challenge is detachment: pulling away when intimacy deepens. Building relationships with room to breathe lets closeness feel safe instead of confining.",
    flow: "Emotional independence feels natural to you. You adapt to change easily and can stay calm when plans fall apart. Unconventional living arrangements or friendships may suit you. Because change rarely unsettles you, you might undervalue stability or struggle to settle when something good comes along. Consistency practised gently can become a real strength.",
    tension: "Your need for closeness and your need for freedom often clash. You might crave intimacy, then feel trapped and withdraw suddenly. Home life may bring disruptions or frequent moves. Anxiety can show as restlessness. Integration involves accepting both needs, communicating clearly about space, and building security that can tolerate change instead of breaking under it."
  },
  "moon|neptune": {
    theme: "Your emotional nature meets boundless sensitivity and imagination. The negotiation is between compassion and self-protection, and between feeling everything around you and knowing which feelings are actually yours.",
    fusion: "You absorb moods like a sponge. Deep empathy, vivid dreams and artistic sensitivity are common. You may be drawn to caring roles or creative work. The difficulty is boundaries: you can take on others' suffering, idealise loved ones, or escape when overwhelmed. Regular solitude, grounding routines and honest self-checking help your compassion remain healthy.",
    flow: "Intuition and emotional sensitivity support each other beautifully. You often sense what others need before they ask, and you may have musical, poetic or healing gifts. Because this attunement comes easily, you might not notice when you are drained, or you may drift into daydreams instead of acting on your insights.",
    tension: "Emotional confusion can arise easily. You might idealise people, feel let down, or struggle to separate your feelings from others'. Escapist habits may tempt when life feels harsh. Home may have felt unclear or unstable in childhood. Integration involves anchoring your sensitivity with clear boundaries and practical self-care so compassion does not cost you yourself."
  },
  "moon|pluto": {
    theme: "Your emotional needs meet intensity, depth and the drive to transform. The negotiation is between trust and control, and between surviving powerful feelings and allowing them to change you.",
    fusion: "Feelings run deep and strong. You may have experienced intense family dynamics early, and emotional life can feel all-or-nothing. Loyalty and perception are remarkable. The shadow side can include jealousy, possessiveness or holding onto hurts. Honest emotional work, perhaps through therapy or journalling, turns this intensity into profound psychological insight and resilience.",
    flow: "You can handle emotional depth without being overwhelmed. Crises often reveal your strength, and people trust you with their secrets. Psychological insight tends to come naturally. Because you manage intensity so well, you may not realise how much you hold back, or you might steer relationships subtly instead of risking open vulnerability.",
    tension: "Powerful emotions can feel threatening, both yours and other people's. You might try to control relationships to avoid being hurt, or find yourself in repeated power struggles at home. Old wounds may resurface. Integration comes through facing fears honestly, releasing grudges, and discovering that genuine intimacy requires letting go of control."
  },
  "moon|chiron": {
    theme: "Your need for nurture meets a tender wound around care and belonging. The negotiation is between protecting that hurt and letting it teach you how to comfort yourself and others.",
    fusion: "Emotional hurt and emotional wisdom live close together in you. Early care may have felt inconsistent, or you may have looked after a parent. This can leave you sensitive to rejection, yet deeply skilled at comforting others. The risk is caring for everyone except yourself. Learning to receive the nurturing you give so freely becomes central to your healing.",
    flow: "Your emotional sensitivity supports your capacity to heal. You tend to listen without judgement, and people feel safe with you. Caring professions or community work may suit you. Because this compassion flows easily, you might overlook your own tender spots. Remember that your insight also applies to your own needs.",
    tension: "Emotional needs can trigger old wounds. You might feel unworthy of care, or push people away before they can let you down. Family patterns may repeat until they are recognised. Integration involves accepting your vulnerability, developing self-compassion, and letting others see where you hurt so that genuine closeness becomes possible."
  },
  "moon|northNode": {
    theme: "Your emotional habits meet the direction of growth your life is reaching toward. The negotiation is whether your comfort zone supports your development or keeps you tied to the familiar.",
    fusion: "Emotional instincts and life direction are closely linked. You often feel called toward growth through family, home, care or public connection. People may sense your emotional authenticity. The challenge is that new territory still feels uncomfortable. Trusting your instincts while staying open to change allows your growth to feel nourishing instead of threatening.",
    flow: "Your emotional nature helps you grow. Supportive relationships and a sense of belonging often open doors, and you intuitively know when to move forward. Because this support feels natural, you might rest in comfort too long. Checking whether your routines still serve your development keeps growth steady.",
    tension: "Comfort and growth can pull in opposite directions. You might feel that meeting emotional needs holds you back, or that pursuing your path costs you security. Family expectations may conflict with your calling. Integration involves taking your need for safety with you into new experiences, instead of choosing one and abandoning the other."
  },
  "moon|lilith": {
    theme: "Your need for closeness meets the part of you that refuses to be tamed. The negotiation is between belonging and authenticity, especially around motherhood, femininity, sexuality and raw emotion.",
    fusion: "Your emotional nature carries a fierce, untamed quality. You may have felt judged for being too emotional or too independent. Motherhood and domestic roles can be complicated territory. This contact gives emotional honesty and an instinct for what others suppress. Allowing yourself to feel fully, without shame, turns this intensity into powerful self-knowledge.",
    flow: "Raw emotions and nurturing instincts work together fairly easily. You can express difficult feelings honestly and hold space for others to do the same. Taboo topics rarely frighten you. Because this comes naturally, you might not notice when your emotional intensity overwhelms more reserved people, or when you are hiding softness behind strength.",
    tension: "Needs for closeness and freedom can clash dramatically. You might feel rejected for your emotional intensity, or suppress anger until it erupts. Relationships with maternal figures may be complicated. Integration comes through accepting both your tender and fierce sides, and finding people who welcome your full emotional range."
  },
  "moon|asc": {
    theme: "Your inner emotional world meets the way you appear to others. The question is how visible your feelings should be, and how much your mood shapes the first impressions you make.",
    fusion: "Feelings show on your face. People often find you approachable, sensitive and easy to read, and you tend to respond instinctively to surroundings. Moods can shift your whole presence. The challenge is exposure: you may feel vulnerable in unfamiliar environments. Developing some trusted routines for difficult days helps you stay open without feeling raw.",
    flow: "Your emotional nature supports how you present yourself. People warm to you quickly, and you can read a room intuitively. You tend to put others at ease. Because this comes naturally, you may not notice how much you adjust to other people's moods, sometimes at the expense of your own.",
    tension: "Inner feelings and outward presentation can seem mismatched. You might hide emotions behind a composed exterior, or feel that others misread you. Partners may carry emotional weight you do not show. Integration involves letting your feelings be seen more honestly, so relationships can meet the real you instead of the persona."
  },
  "moon|mc": {
    theme: "Your need for security meets your public ambitions and reputation. The negotiation is between home and career, and between private emotional life and the role you play in the world.",
    fusion: "Emotional needs and public life are closely linked. You may be drawn to careers involving care, food, property or public service, and people often sense your warmth professionally. Your reputation can fluctuate with your moods. Building emotional security outside work helps you enjoy recognition without depending on it.",
    flow: "Your emotional nature supports your career. Work that feels meaningful comes fairly naturally, and you can create a sense of family in professional settings. Because this integration feels easy, you might not notice when work demands crowd out personal needs. Protecting time at home keeps this balance healthy.",
    tension: "Home and career can compete. You might feel torn between family responsibilities and ambition, or experience career changes driven by emotional needs. Public roles may feel exposing. Integration comes when you define success in ways that honour emotional wellbeing, and allow both home and work to support each other."
  },
  "mercury|venus": {
    theme: "Thought and taste have to cooperate. Mercury shapes how you speak and reason, Venus what you find beautiful and how you relate, and together they set the tone of your conversations and creative expression.",
    fusion: "You tend to speak graciously and think in terms of harmony. Words, design, music or diplomacy may come naturally, and people often find your manner pleasant and persuasive. You may be drawn to writing, art or mediation. The shadow is a tendency to say what people want to hear, softening truths that need to be heard plainly.",
    flow: "Only a sextile is possible between these two, and it gives a light, graceful touch with words. You can deliver difficult messages kindly and often charm others in conversation. Creative writing, design or negotiation may suit you. Because tact comes easily, you might avoid necessary bluntness, or settle for pretty expression when deeper substance is called for.",
    tension: "Squares cannot form here, so any strain is mild, perhaps a gap between what you think and what you feel comfortable saying. You might agree outwardly while privately disagreeing, or intellectualise matters of the heart. Integration involves practising honesty that is also kind, letting both your mind and your values have a voice."
  },
  "mercury|mars": {
    theme: "Your mind meets your drive, so thinking and acting have to agree on speed and tone. The question is whether your words become sharp tools or careless weapons.",
    fusion: "Your mind moves fast and your words carry force. You often argue well, think quickly on your feet, and enjoy debate. People may experience you as direct or even blunt. The risk is impatience and a sharp tongue when frustrated. Pausing before you respond, especially in writing, lets your mental courage work for you instead of burning bridges.",
    flow: "Quick thinking and decisive action support each other. You tend to solve problems promptly, speak up without fear, and turn ideas into plans efficiently. Debate, sport commentary, engineering or trade may suit you. Because mental energy comes easily, you might skip careful reflection, or win arguments without really listening to the other side.",
    tension: "Your thoughts and temper can collide. Arguments may escalate quickly, and you might say things you later regret. Nervous energy can show as restlessness or impatience. In relationships, discussions can turn into battles. Integration involves channelling mental intensity into constructive debate, physical activity or problem-solving, and learning to listen as sharply as you speak."
  },
  "mercury|jupiter": {
    theme: "Your mind meets the drive to expand, believe and understand the big picture. The negotiation is between detail and vision, and between precise facts and larger meaning.",
    fusion: "You think big and speak with enthusiasm. Learning, travel, languages and philosophy may fascinate you, and you often inspire others with ideas. People may see you as a natural teacher. The shadow is exaggeration or overconfidence in opinions, and a tendency to overlook details. Balancing enthusiasm with careful checking makes your ideas genuinely persuasive.",
    flow: "Your mind is broad, generous and optimistic. You tend to learn easily, communicate hopefully, and connect ideas across fields. Teaching, publishing, law or travel can suit you. Because understanding comes readily, you might skim instead of studying deeply, or assume you know enough to speak with authority on things you have barely explored.",
    tension: "Details and big ideas can fight for attention. You might overcommit mentally, promise too much, or struggle to finish studies you started with enthusiasm. Opinions may clash with others' beliefs. Integration involves grounding your wide vision in thorough research, and remaining curious enough to revise beliefs when better information appears."
  },
  "mercury|saturn": {
    theme: "Your mind meets the demand for structure, rigour and caution. The negotiation is between speaking freely and speaking carefully, and between curiosity and the fear of getting things wrong.",
    fusion: "Your thinking is serious, precise and cautious. You may have felt misunderstood early, or doubted your intelligence, and this often led you to study hard. Over time, you can become an authority in your field. The risk is pessimism or rigid thinking. Allowing yourself to speak before your ideas are perfect keeps your mind flexible and alive.",
    flow: "Discipline supports your mind naturally. You tend to think systematically, plan well and communicate clearly. Accounting, science, editing or anything requiring careful analysis may suit you. Because structure feels comfortable, you might stay in familiar mental territory, dismissing creative or intuitive ideas that do not fit your established frameworks.",
    tension: "Self-doubt about your intellect can hold you back. You might fear speaking up, criticise yourself harshly, or struggle with learning difficulties that shaped early confidence. Communication may feel effortful or blocked. Integration comes through steady practice, recognising your competence, and letting your caution serve accuracy instead of silencing you."
  },
  "mercury|uranus": {
    theme: "Your mind meets the flash of insight and the urge to break rules. The negotiation is between originality and coherence, and between brilliant leaps and explaining them clearly to others.",
    fusion: "Your mind works in sudden flashes. You often think ahead of your time, and you may be drawn to technology, science, astrology or anything unconventional. Conversation with you can be exhilarating and unpredictable. The challenge is nervous tension and impatience with slower thinkers. Grounding insights with patient explanation helps others follow your leaps.",
    flow: "Original thinking comes easily. You tend to see new solutions, adapt quickly to technology, and communicate inventive ideas in ways others can grasp. Because inspiration arrives readily, you may not follow through, jumping to the next idea before the last has taken shape. Some structure turns brilliance into results.",
    tension: "Your mind can race, scatter or rebel against conventional thinking. You might struggle with routine study, clash with authorities over ideas, or experience anxiety from overstimulation. People may find you contrary. Integration involves channelling restless brilliance into focused projects, and developing patience to explain insights instead of dismissing those who disagree."
  },
  "mercury|neptune": {
    theme: "Your rational mind meets imagination, intuition and ambiguity. The negotiation is between clarity and inspiration, and between precise facts and the images, symbols and feelings that also carry truth.",
    fusion: "Your mind is poetic and intuitive. You may think in images, pick up on unspoken feelings, and be gifted in music, fiction or spiritual study. Logic can feel less natural. The risk is confusion, forgetfulness or being easily misled. Writing things down, checking facts, and giving your imagination a creative outlet keeps this gift clear.",
    flow: "Imagination and thought blend gracefully. You tend to communicate with sensitivity, and creative writing, music, photography or healing work may suit you. Intuitive understanding often comes easily. Because it comes so readily, you might rely on impressions instead of verifying details, or drift into daydreams when practical tasks need attention.",
    tension: "Clarity can blur under pressure. You might misunderstand others, feel misunderstood, or be drawn into deception, either as the one deceived or through vague half-truths. Concentration may wander. Integration involves grounding intuition with careful checking, being honest even when it is uncomfortable, and using imagination deliberately instead of as an escape."
  },
  "mercury|pluto": {
    theme: "Your mind meets depth, intensity and the drive to uncover what is hidden. The negotiation is between insight and obsession, and between words that heal and words that wound.",
    fusion: "Your thinking is penetrating and investigative. You tend to dig beneath surfaces, keep secrets well, and communicate with persuasive power. Research, psychology or detective work may suit you. The shadow is obsessive thinking or using words to control. Choosing curiosity over suspicion helps you use your insight to empower instead of manipulate.",
    flow: "Depth of thought comes naturally. You can analyse complex problems, understand motivations, and speak with quiet authority. People often seek your perspective in a crisis. Because this insight feels ordinary to you, you might underestimate its impact on others, or avoid sharing what you see for fear of its intensity.",
    tension: "Thoughts can become obsessive or suspicious. You might engage in intellectual power struggles, or feel that information is being withheld from you. Words can wound deeply when you are hurt. Integration involves turning your penetrating mind toward self-understanding, releasing the need to win arguments, and speaking hard truths with care."
  },
  "mercury|chiron": {
    theme: "Your mind and voice meet a sore spot around being heard, understood or thought clever enough. The negotiation is between protecting that hurt and letting it become insight you can share.",
    fusion: "Communication and woundedness are closely linked. You may have felt misunderstood, struggled with learning, or had your voice dismissed early. This often makes you an attentive listener and a thoughtful teacher, because you know what confusion feels like. The risk is self-censorship. Speaking even when unsure lets your insight reach the people who need it.",
    flow: "Your mind and your wisdom support each other gently. You often find words that help people feel understood, and teaching, counselling or writing may come easily. Because this empathy flows naturally, you might keep helping others articulate their pain while leaving your own story unspoken.",
    tension: "Old wounds around intelligence or voice can resurface. You might fear sounding foolish, overprepare, or become defensive when challenged. Misunderstandings may cut deeper than expected. Integration involves recognising where early criticism still shapes your thinking, practising self-expression gently, and treating your mistakes as part of learning instead of evidence of failure."
  },
  "mercury|northNode": {
    theme: "Your thinking and communication meet the direction of growth your life is reaching toward. The negotiation is whether your habits of mind support development or keep you stuck in familiar ideas.",
    fusion: "Your mind is closely tied to your growth. Learning, writing, teaching or networking often become part of your purpose. People may see you as a messenger or connector. The challenge is that growth still requires uncomfortable new ideas. Staying curious and open lets your intellectual gifts guide you toward meaningful new territory.",
    flow: "Your communication skills support your development. Conversations and learning often open doors, and you tend to meet helpful people through ideas. Because this happens easily, you might keep gathering information without acting on it. Choosing a direction and following through turns your gifts into real progress.",
    tension: "Thinking habits can pull away from growth. You might overanalyse decisions, or cling to familiar opinions when your path calls for a new perspective. Communication may feel at odds with where you are heading. Integration involves questioning old mental patterns and letting learning lead you somewhere unfamiliar."
  },
  "mercury|lilith": {
    theme: "Your mind and voice meet the untamed truths that polite society prefers to ignore. The negotiation is between speaking freely and staying accepted, especially on taboo subjects.",
    fusion: "Your mind is provocative and unafraid of forbidden topics. You may have been silenced or punished for saying the wrong thing, and now you tend to speak what others avoid. This can make you a sharp writer or critic. The risk is using words to shock instead of illuminate. Choosing your moments gives your truths more impact.",
    flow: "Raw honesty and communication work together fairly easily. You can discuss sexuality, anger, injustice or shadow material without much discomfort, which helps others open up. Because this comes naturally, you might not notice when bluntness hurts, or when you are using edginess to avoid vulnerability.",
    tension: "What you think and what you dare to say may clash. You might censor yourself heavily, then burst out with harsh words. Taboo thoughts may cause shame. Integration comes through claiming your right to speak difficult truths, finding safe places to explore them, and delivering them with both courage and care."
  },
  "mercury|asc": {
    theme: "Your mind meets the way you present yourself. The question is how much your curiosity, wit and words shape the first impression you create and the way others experience you.",
    fusion: "You come across as quick, curious and talkative. People notice your mind first, and you often engage through conversation. You may appear younger than your years. The challenge is nervousness or restlessness, especially in new situations. Taking time to listen as well as speak helps others see the depth behind your quick manner.",
    flow: "Your thinking and self-presentation cooperate smoothly. You tend to make a good impression through words, and people find you easy to talk to. Networking, teaching or sales may come naturally. Because this charm is effortless, you might rely on verbal agility instead of building deeper knowledge or listening closely.",
    tension: "Thoughts and self-presentation can clash. You might feel misunderstood when you speak, or come across as more nervous or argumentative than you intend. Partners may challenge your ideas often. Integration involves slowing down, clarifying what you really mean, and letting your manner reflect your thinking more honestly."
  },
  "mercury|mc": {
    theme: "Your mind meets your public role and career direction. The negotiation is between intellectual interests and professional ambitions, and between what you know and what you are recognised for.",
    fusion: "Your career is likely tied to communication, ideas or information. Writing, teaching, media, sales or technology may suit you, and people often know you for your intelligence. The risk is identifying too closely with your professional reputation for being clever. Continuing to learn keeps your public voice fresh and credible.",
    flow: "Your mental skills support your career naturally. You can articulate goals clearly, and professional opportunities often arise through networking or writing. Because this comes easily, you might not push toward work that fully uses your intellect. Seeking out harder problems, or a role with more intellectual stretch, keeps your professional growth meaningful.",
    tension: "Intellectual interests and career demands may pull apart. You might feel your job does not use your mind, or that your ideas are dismissed publicly. Communication with authority figures can be strained. Integration involves finding work that values your thinking, and learning to present ideas in ways decision-makers can hear."
  },
  "venus|mars": {
    theme: "Attraction and desire, receptivity and pursuit, have to find their balance. Venus draws people toward you and Mars goes after what it wants, so together they shape your romantic and sexual chemistry.",
    fusion: "Passion runs strong in you. You tend to be magnetic, sensual and creatively energetic, and relationships can feel exciting from the start. Love and desire blend easily. The challenge is impulsiveness: falling fast, acting on attraction before checking compatibility, or mixing affection with conflict. Pacing your passions lets them deepen instead of burning out.",
    flow: "Romance and assertion cooperate gracefully. You can pursue what you want without losing charm, and relationships usually balance give and take. Creative and artistic work may flow easily. Because attraction comes naturally, you might take chemistry for granted and neglect the effort long-term partnerships need.",
    tension: "What attracts you and what you desire can pull apart. You might want someone who does not suit you, or feel torn between harmony and passion. Relationships may swing between closeness and conflict. Integration involves recognising both your need for connection and your need for excitement, and choosing partners who can meet both."
  },
  "venus|jupiter": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love and pleasure meets the urge to expand and enjoy abundantly. The negotiation is between generosity and indulgence, and between appreciation and always wanting more.",
    fusion: "Warmth and generosity come naturally. You tend to enjoy life, attract goodwill, and love beauty, art and good company. People often feel welcome around you. The shadow is overindulgence in food, spending or romance. Finding pleasure in quality instead of quantity lets this genuinely lucky contact bring lasting satisfaction.",
    flow: "Good fortune often touches your relationships and finances. You tend to be sociable, optimistic and appreciative, and people are drawn to your easy warmth. Because this comes so naturally, you might coast on charm, or avoid difficult conversations that would make your relationships stronger and more honest over time.",
    tension: "Your desires can outrun your resources. You might overspend, overcommit socially, or idealise partners and then feel disappointed. Values may clash with beliefs. Integration involves finding contentment in what you already have, developing sensible limits around pleasure, and letting your generosity be wise as well as warm."
  },
  "venus|saturn": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love and pleasure meets caution, commitment and the passage of time. The negotiation is between enjoying life freely and taking relationships seriously enough to build something lasting.",
    fusion: "Love tends to be serious business for you. You may have felt unworthy of affection early, or experienced delays in relationships. Loyalty and commitment run deep. You might attract older partners or find love later. The challenge is fear of rejection. Allowing yourself to enjoy love lightly sometimes helps loosen the protective armour you carry.",
    flow: "Stability supports your relationships and values. You tend to choose partners carefully, manage money wisely, and appreciate classic, lasting beauty. People trust your loyalty. Because commitment comes naturally, you might stay in relationships that have become more duty than joy, or play safe in matters of taste and romance.",
    tension: "Love and fear often intertwine. You might feel lonely even in company, doubt your attractiveness, or hold back affection until you feel secure. Relationships can bring lessons about self-worth. Integration involves valuing yourself independently of others' approval, and allowing love to grow gradually into something you trust."
  },
  "venus|uranus": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love meets the urge for freedom, excitement and originality. The negotiation is between intimacy and independence, and between stable affection and the thrill of the new.",
    fusion: "Love tends to arrive suddenly and unconventionally. You are often attracted to unusual people, and you may need a lot of space within relationships. Your taste in art and style can be distinctive. The challenge is commitment. Creating partnerships with room for individuality lets you enjoy stability without feeling caged.",
    flow: "Freedom and affection coexist comfortably. You tend to attract interesting people, enjoy friendships with former partners, and bring creativity into relationships. Your aesthetic sense can be innovative. Because this comes easily, you might avoid the deeper commitment that would give your relationships real roots, moving on just as things become meaningful.",
    tension: "Desire for closeness and desire for freedom can clash. Relationships may begin or end suddenly, and you might feel restless as soon as things become settled. Partners may experience you as unpredictable. Integration involves discussing needs for space openly, and learning that commitment and independence can support each other."
  },
  "venus|neptune": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love meets idealism, imagination and the longing for perfect union. The negotiation is between romantic vision and seeing people clearly as they really are.",
    fusion: "Romance and imagination blend powerfully. You tend to idealise love, respond to music and beauty deeply, and may have real artistic talent. Compassion runs strong. The risk is falling for potential instead of reality, or sacrificing yourself for love. Grounding your dreams in honest assessment protects your tender heart.",
    flow: "Artistic sensitivity and compassion come naturally. You may have gifts in music, dance, film or design, and people often find you gentle and understanding. Because inspiration flows easily, you might not develop the skill to match your vision, or you may avoid the practical side of relationships.",
    tension: "Love can feel confusing or disappointing. You might idealise partners, then feel betrayed when they turn out to be human, or give too much of yourself. Deception or escapism can enter relationships. Integration comes through keeping compassion but setting boundaries, seeing people clearly, and finding the sacred in ordinary, imperfect love."
  },
  "venus|pluto": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love meets intensity, power and transformation. The negotiation is between deep passion and control, and between wholehearted devotion and the fear of losing yourself.",
    fusion: "Love for you is all or nothing. You tend to attract intense relationships that transform you, and your magnetism can be striking. Jealousy or possessiveness may appear when you feel insecure. Learning to trust without controlling, and to release relationships that have ended, allows your passion to heal instead of consume.",
    flow: "Depth and intimacy come naturally. You can form profound bonds, sense hidden dynamics, and regenerate after heartbreak. People often feel truly seen by you. Because this intensity is familiar, you might not notice when you overwhelm others, or when you are drawn to drama for its own sake.",
    tension: "Love can become a battleground. You might experience power struggles, obsessive attractions or painful endings. Fear of vulnerability can lead to control or manipulation, on either side. Integration involves examining your patterns honestly, releasing old wounds, and allowing love to transform you without needing to possess the other person."
  },
  "venus|chiron": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love and self-worth meets a tender wound. The negotiation is between protecting yourself from rejection and learning to value yourself as you are, scars included.",
    fusion: "Love and hurt are closely linked for you. You may have felt unlovable or unattractive at some point, and this sensitivity can make you deeply compassionate toward others. You might be drawn to healing through art or beauty. The challenge is believing you are worthy. Self-kindness gradually transforms this wound into grace.",
    flow: "Your sensitivity supports your relationships gently. You often understand others' insecurities, and people feel accepted by you. Art, beauty or counselling may become ways you heal. Because this compassion comes naturally, you might neglect your own need for care. Accepting love as readily as you give it matters.",
    tension: "Self-worth wounds can surface in relationships. You might attract partners who reopen old hurts, or doubt your value despite evidence. Comparison can sting. Integration involves recognising patterns rooted in early rejection, treating yourself with tenderness, and choosing relationships and friendships that honour your full worth."
  },
  "venus|northNode": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love and your values meet the direction of growth your life is reaching toward. The negotiation is whether relationships and pleasure help you develop or keep you comfortable.",
    fusion: "Love and life direction are closely linked. Relationships, art or values often play a central role in your growth. Important partnerships may feel fated. The risk is relying on others to move you forward. Developing your own sense of worth ensures relationships support your path instead of defining it.",
    flow: "Relationships and pleasures tend to support your growth. You meet helpful people easily, and creative or social interests often open doors. Because this happens gracefully, you might settle into comfortable connections instead of seeking those that stretch you. Choosing relationships consciously, including ones that challenge you, keeps growth alive.",
    tension: "What you enjoy and what helps you grow can pull apart. You might cling to relationships that hold you back, or feel that pursuing your purpose costs you love. Integration involves aligning your values with your path, and trusting that growth can include pleasure and connection instead of sacrificing them."
  },
  "venus|lilith": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love meets raw, untamed desire. The negotiation is between being agreeable and being authentic, especially around sexuality, attraction and what you are willing to compromise.",
    fusion: "Your attractiveness carries a wild, magnetic quality. You may have been judged for your sexuality or desires, and you tend to reject conventional ideas about love. Relationships can be intense. The challenge is integrating sweetness and fierceness. Owning your desires without shame lets you form relationships where your full self is welcome.",
    flow: "Sensuality and authenticity blend easily. You can express desire confidently and talk openly about intimacy, which helps others do the same. Your style may be distinctive. Because this comes naturally, you might not notice when you use allure to avoid deeper vulnerability, or when others feel pressured by your openness.",
    tension: "Desire for harmony and raw desire can clash. You might suppress your wild side to be liked, then feel resentful, or attract relationships that trigger shame. Integration involves recognising that you can be loving and untamed at once, and choosing partners who honour both your softness and your fire."
  },
  "venus|asc": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love and beauty meets the way you present yourself. The question is how much charm and grace shape your first impressions, and how much you rely on them.",
    fusion: "You tend to come across as attractive, pleasant and graceful. People warm to you easily, and you may care about appearance and style. Social situations often flow smoothly. The shadow is people-pleasing or relying too much on charm. Letting others see your less polished sides helps them connect with the real you.",
    flow: "Grace and approachability come naturally. You tend to create a harmonious atmosphere, and people often feel comfortable around you quickly. Because charm comes easily, you might avoid conflict, or rely on appearances instead of developing substance and honest communication. Friends may not realise how much effort you put into keeping everyone comfortable.",
    tension: "The wish to be liked and your authentic self can clash. You might feel pressure to look or act a certain way, or attract partners who value your image more than your character. Integration involves letting your values shape your presentation, and discovering that authenticity is its own kind of beauty."
  },
  "venus|mc": {
    theme: "Your capacity for love and beauty meets your public role and ambitions. The negotiation is between pleasure and career, and between being liked and being respected.",
    fusion: "Your career may involve beauty, art, diplomacy or relationships. People often see you as gracious in public, and professional success can come through charm and good relationships. The risk is prioritising popularity over integrity. Grounding your public image in genuine values keeps your reputation solid.",
    flow: "Grace supports your career naturally. You tend to work well with others, attract helpful contacts, and bring beauty into your professional life. Because this happens easily, you might not push for the recognition you deserve. Asking for promotions, fair pay and credit for your work keeps your career growing.",
    tension: "Personal pleasures and career demands can conflict. You might feel torn between relationships and ambitions, or experience public criticism of your values. Integration involves aligning work with what you truly love, and building a reputation that reflects your genuine character instead of a pleasing image."
  }
};
